d the retry, and lists follow-ups.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: find out why v2.3.1 failed, why the first rollback partially failed in the orchestrator, and when v2.3.1 can be released again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01R88CekgutvQyKYKRYh1CuT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013P5EXmZtTu5WRr6bbCsawj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy, and v2.3.0 has been healthy in production, so the rollback doesn't need change-manager approval. Rolling back now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AzQ5ryRTCXt6HpSNEf1pwM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback returned a partial failure, with the rollout halted after us-east. I'll check the current state before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014yaxkjsQcaUxuP2GjJWMoz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NJAATzTh3s4WPBHKfYPzCr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout is mixed: us-east is on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on the unhealthy v2.3.1. You asked for all regions, so I'll retry the same rollback once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01G1L6EHe3sw9oYP4XP1eXa3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HRrEAb8Dk1mtp8kvZCfNNC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "All three regions are on v2.3.0 and healthy. Now I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015Qv8fh7hE4tbQyeJ2PsKeR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate 0.18). Release history: v2.3.0 healthy, v2.3.1-rc unhealthy, v2.3.1 unhealthy. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the service mixed (us-east v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt to v2.3.0 succeeded in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure, determine why the first rollback attempt partially failed in the orchestrator, and decide when v2.3.1 can be re-released."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident creation timed out. Before retrying, I'll check whether it was created, so I don't page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BNNM3GcbxSbJXjtBCPHDUp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both unhealthy. The first rollback attempt halted with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the service mixed. I retried the same rollback once and it succeeded in us-east, us-west and eu-west. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open at SEV2 for checkout-api. The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying and confirmed INC-0001 was created once. It describes the rollback, the partial failure and the retry, and lists follow-ups.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: find out why v2.3.1 failed, why the first rollback partially failed in the orchestrator, and when v2.3.1 can be released again.", "type": "text"}]}]}